    "q-169991": {
      "dom_id": "step-q169991",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4r+9v=3 \\\\ 8r-2v=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $r$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-2$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-8r-18v & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=-5.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nWhat's the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the first equation by $-2$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,4r+9v=3\\,)\\,\\times (-2) \\\\ 8r-2v=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-8r-18v=-6 \\\\ 8r-2v=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{8r}-18v & =-6 \\\\ \\cancel{8r}-2v & =1 \\\\ (-2v-18v) & =(1-6) \\\\ -20v & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $-20v.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
