    "q-214923": {
      "dom_id": "step-q214923",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-12 \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $x$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-1$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-x+5y & =12.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$=32.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the first equation by $-1$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,x-5y=-12\\,)\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+5y=12 \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{x}+5y & =12 \\\\ \\cancel{x}+3y & =20 \\\\ (5y+3y) & =(12+20) \\\\ 8y & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
