    "q-214930": {
      "dom_id": "step-q214930",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+7y=-20 \\\\ 4x-y=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $7$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}28x-7y=-49.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$=-69.$\n\n$\\,$\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $($\n{{field-2}}$\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the second equation by $7$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+7y=-20 \\\\ (\\,4x-y=-7\\,)\\,\\times (7)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+7y=-20 \\\\ 28x-7y=-49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $y,$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5x+\\cancel{7y} & =-20 \\\\ 28x-\\cancel{7y} & =-49 \\\\ (-5x+28x) & =(-20-49) \\\\ 23x & =-69\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $x=-3.$ However, we still need to find $y.$ To do this, we substitute $x=-3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-y & =-7 \\\\ 4(-3)-y & =-7 \\\\ -12-y & =-7 \\\\ -y & =5 \\\\ y & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-3,\\,y=-5,$ which can be expressed as $(\\,-3,-5\\,).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
