    "q-170011": {
      "dom_id": "step-q170011",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u+5p=24 \\\\ 5u+p=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $p$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $-5$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-25u-5p=-45.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=-21.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(u,p)$ of the system.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's follow the steps provided:\n\n**Step 1**: Multiplying the second equation by $-5$ yields the following equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u+5p=24 \\\\ (\\,5u+p=9\\,)\\,\\times (-5)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4u+5p=24 \\\\ -25u-5p=-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we add these two equations together, *eliminate* the variable $p,$ and solve the resulting equation for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4u+\\cancel{5p} & =24 \\\\ -25u-\\cancel{5p} & =-45 \\\\ (4u-25u) & =(24-45) \\\\ -21u & =-21 \\\\ u & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $u=1.$ However, we still need to find $p.$ To do this, we substitute $u=1$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5u+p & =9 \\\\ 5(1)+p & =9 \\\\ 5+p & =9 \\\\ p & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=1,\\,p=4,$ which can be expressed as $(1,4).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
